   "text": "You see, a ship stays upright like a weighted toy: heavy at the bottom, light at the top. The Vasa was the opposite. Its bronze cannons sat high on two decks, over just 120 tons of stone. It needed about twice as much, but more weight would push the lower gun ports down to the waterline. So when thirty men ran across the deck, the ship was already warning them.",
   "role": "",
   "key": 2,
